WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
Octane is a fuel built from just
two elements: carbon and hydrogen.

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.400
On paper, it burns to
carbon dioxide and water.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.740
Yet engine exhaust carries pollutants,
and some of them are toxic.

4
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.540
If the fuel holds only
carbon and hydrogen,

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.160
where do those poisonous gases come from?

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.060
In this mission, you'll see why
alkanes make such good fuels,

7
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.580
and write balanced
equations for burning them.

8
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:30.360
Then you'll trace what leaves the engine,
gas by gas, and find out why it matters.

9
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.770
Your mission: find out where the
poisonous gases in exhaust come from.